# theCollider Pro -- BIP-39 / BIP-32 candidate phrases.
#
# One mnemonic phrase per line. Words separated by whitespace.
# Phrase length: 12, 15, 18, 21, or 24 words (BIP-39 standard).
# Lines starting with '#' or blank lines are skipped.
#
# To start using this file: rename it from
#   wordlists/bip_phrases.txt.example
# to
#   wordlists/bip_phrases.txt
# and replace the lines below with your own candidate phrases.
#
# Examples (these are FAMOUS test mnemonics from the BIP-39 spec;
# they are NOT funded, but they let you verify the scanner runs):

abandon abandon abandon abandon abandon abandon abandon abandon abandon abandon abandon about
legal winner thank year wave sausage worth useful legal winner thank yellow
letter advice cage absurd amount doctor acoustic avoid letter advice cage above
zoo zoo zoo zoo zoo zoo zoo zoo zoo zoo zoo zoo zoo zoo zoo zoo zoo zoo zoo zoo zoo zoo zoo wrong
